    {
      "beat_id": "B05POLICY",
      "act": "SHOW",
      "heading": "Learning from experience",
      "narration_text": "The agent's rule for choosing moves is called its policy. During training, a learning algorithm uses observations, actions and rewards to improve that policy, either directly or by first learning which actions tend to pay off. Sometimes it tries an unfamiliar move just to see what happens. That's the balance between exploring and exploiting.",
