    {
      "beat_id": "B06TEST",
      "act": "SHOW",
      "heading": "Testing and takeaway",
      "narration_text": "Because Gymnasium environments share one interface, researchers can run the same training code on many of them. To check whether learning carries over, they test the policy on situations it never practiced. With CoinRun, researchers set game levels aside for testing and found that agents overfit even to very large sets of training levels. My own project holds back a set of worlds for the same reason. So when someone says an agent has learned a task, ask two things: what was it rewarded for, and what was held back for the test? So an RL environment is the world an agent practices in: it sets the rules, hands out the rewards, and decides when an episode ends. Thanks for watching.",
